# Enemy AI System for Pimpa-Raka

# This rule documents the enemy AI architecture for creating and extending enemy behaviors.
# Reference: scripts/enemies/README_ENEMY_AI.md for complete documentation.

# ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW
# ====================
# The enemy system uses a state machine with vision-based detection and personality parameters.
#
# Enemy.gd (CharacterBody2D)
# ├── Vision System (line-of-sight, vision cones)
# ├── Awareness System (buildup/decay, last known position)
# ├── Personality System (aggression, caution, persistence)
# └── StateMachine
#     ├── idle (patrol)
#     ├── suspicious (investigating)
#     ├── chase (pursuing player)
#     ├── attack (telegraph → strike → recovery)
#     ├── search (looking for lost player)
#     └── hurt (stagger reaction)

# STATE TRANSITIONS
# =================
# idle → suspicious: Peripheral vision detects player
# idle → chase: Direct vision sees player
# suspicious → chase: Found player or awareness threshold reached
# suspicious → idle: Timeout with no evidence
# chase → attack: Player on same level and in attack range
# chase → search: Lost line of sight
# attack → chase: Attack complete, player moved away
# search → chase: Found player again
# search → idle: Search timeout
# Any state → hurt: Took damage
# hurt → chase: Recovery complete (enemy becomes angry)

# VISION SYSTEM
# =============
# Direct Vision:
#   - Range: vision_range (default 120px)
#   - Angle: vision_angle (default 60° half-angle)
#   - Blocked by terrain (raycast check)
#   - Triggers immediate alert
#
# Peripheral Vision:
#   - Range: peripheral_range (default 60px)
#   - Angle: peripheral_angle (default 120° half-angle)
#   - Triggers suspicion, not immediate chase
#
# Key functions:
#   - can_see_player() → bool: Direct vision check
#   - can_see_player_peripheral() → bool: Peripheral check
#   - _raycast_to_player() → bool: Line of sight clear

# AWARENESS SYSTEM
# ================
# awareness_level: 0.0 (unaware) to 2.0 (hyper-alert)
#   - 0.0-0.5: Suspicious, looking around
#   - 0.5-1.0: Alert, actively investigating
#   - 1.0+: Combat mode
#   - 2.0: After being hit (maximum alertness)
#
# Buildup/Decay rates controlled by:
#   - suspicion_buildup_rate (default 2.0)
#   - suspicion_decay_rate (default 0.5)
#   - Personality affects these values
#
# last_known_player_position: Updated when player seen, used for search behavior

# PERSONALITY SYSTEM
# ==================
# Three parameters (0.0 to 1.0) affect enemy behavior:
#
# aggression (default 0.5):
#   - Higher: Faster chase, shorter attack telegraph, more aggressive
#   - Lower: Slower, longer warning before attacks
#
# caution (default 0.5):
#   - Higher: Shorter effective vision range
#   - Lower: Longer vision range
#
# persistence (default 0.5):
#   - Higher: Searches longer, awareness decays slower
#   - Lower: Gives up quickly, awareness decays fast

# ATTACK TELEGRAPH SYSTEM
# =======================
# Three phases ensure fair, readable combat:
#
# 1. TELEGRAPH (default 0.3s, reduced by aggression):
#    - Enemy stops moving
#    - Visual warning (pulsing color or animation)
#    - Player has time to react
#
# 2. STRIKE (default 0.2s):
#    - Enemy lunges at 1.5x speed
#    - Damage dealt at 30% into phase
#    - One hit per attack cycle
#
# 3. RECOVERY (default 0.4s):
#    - Enemy slows down
#    - Vulnerability window
#    - Cannot attack again until complete

# CREATING NEW ENEMY TYPES
# ========================
# Method 1: Inspector Configuration
#   1. Duplicate Enemy.tscn
#   2. Adjust exported parameters in Inspector
#   3. Change enemy_color for visual distinction
#
# Method 2: Script Extension
#   ```gdscript
#   class_name FastEnemy
#   extends Enemy
#
#   func _ready():
#       speed = 30.0
#       aggression = 0.9
#       caution = 0.1
#       super._ready()
#   ```

